triggers.BalintHelper/BaseInstructionTrigger/AllocInstruction.placements.description.main=- nuint 'size' is pushed onto the stack\n- 'size' is popped from the stack and a zeroed native memory of the specified size is allocated\n- pushes the UIntPtr result onto the stack.\nNote: The memory is freed when the method exits.
triggers.BalintHelper/ArithmeticInstructionTrigger.placements.description.main=- object 'X' (or for binary operations 'X' and 'Y') is pushed onto the stack\n- The object(s) are popped from the stack, converted to dynamic, and the specified operation is performed.\n- The result is pushed onto the stack.
triggers.BalintHelper/BaseInstructionTrigger/ArrayGetLengthInstruction.placements.description.main=- an array instance is pushed onto the stack\n- an int 'rank' is pushed onto the stack\n- The array and 'rank' are popped from the stack\n- the specified rank's length is pushed onto the stack.
triggers.BalintHelper/BaseInstructionTrigger/ArrayRankInstruction.placements.description.main=- an array instance is pushed onto the stack\n- The array is popped from the stack and it's rank is queried\n- The rank is pushed onto the stack.
triggers.BalintHelper/BaseInstructionTrigger/ArrayVectorLengthInstruction.placements.description.main=- an array of rank 1 is pushed onto the stack\n- The array is popped from the stack and it's length is queried\n- The length is pushed onto the stack.
triggers.BalintHelper/CastInstructionTrigger/CastInstruction.placements.description.main=- an object 'X' is pushed onto the stack\n- 'X' is popped from the stack, and converted to the type of the cast instruction (with an optional source type)\n- The cast object is pushed onto the stack.
triggers.BalintHelper/CompareInstructionTrigger.placements.description.main=- object 'X' and object 'Y' are pushed onto the stack\n- 'X' and 'Y' are popped from the stack, converted to dynamic, and the comparison is performed.\n- The resulting boolean is pushed onto the stack.
triggers.BalintHelper/ConditionalInstructionTrigger/ConditionalInstruction.placements.description.main=- boolean 'B' is pushed onto the stack\n- 'B' is popped from the stack, and if 'B' was 'true', a branch operation is performed.\n- If 'B' was 'false', the next instruction is executed instead.
triggers.BalintHelper/BaseInstructionTrigger/DupInstruction.placements.description.main=- an object 'X' is pushed onto the stack\n- 'X' is popped from the stack\n- 'X' gets pushed onto the stack exactly twice.
triggers.BalintHelper/GetComponentTrigger/NopInstruction.placements.description.main=- an entity 'E' is pushed onto the stack\n- 'E' is popped from the stack and the component of the specified type is queried\n- The component is pushed onto the stack.
triggers.BalintHelper/GetConstructorInfoTrigger/LoadConstantInstruction.placements.description.main=- pushes the constructor stored within the instruction onto the stack\nNote: to actually call it, use Invoke
triggers.BalintHelper/GetDynamicMethodInfoTrigger/LoadConstantInstruction.placements.description.main=- pushes the dynamic method info stored within the instruction onto the stack\nNote: to actually call it, use Invoke
triggers.BalintHelper/GetEntityInfoTrigger/LoadConstantInstruction.placements.description.main=- pushes the entity filter stored within the instruction onto the stack\nNote: to actually get an entity list, use either Read or Invoke
triggers.BalintHelper/GetFieldInfoTrigger/LoadConstantInstruction.placements.description.main=- pushes the field stored within the instruction onto the stack\nNote: to read or write the value, use Read or Write
triggers.BalintHelper/GetMethodInfoTrigger/LoadConstantInstruction.placements.description.main=- pushes the method stored within the instruction onto the stack\nNote: to actually call it, use Invoke
triggers.BalintHelper/GetPropertyInfoTrigger/LoadConstantInstruction.placements.description.main=- pushes the property stored within the instruction onto the stack\nNote: to actually read or write the value, use Read or Write (or for indexers, ReadIndexer/WriteIndexer)
triggers.BalintHelper/GetSceneTrigger/NopInstruction.placements.description.main=- queries the current Engine.Scene instance\n- The result is pushed onto the stack.
triggers.BalintHelper/GetRandomTrigger/NopInstruction.placements.description.main=- queries the seeded Random instance\n- The result is pushed onto the stack.
triggers.BalintHelper/GetSessionInfoTrigger/LoadConstantInstruction.placements.description.main=- pushes the session variable info stored within the instruction onto the stack\nNote: to actually read or write the value, use Read or Write
triggers.BalintHelper/GetSfxEventInfoTrigger/LoadConstantInstruction.placements.description.main=- pushes the audio stored within the instruction onto the stack\nNote: to actually call it, use Invoke\nUsage:\n- the audio position (or null) is pushed onto the stack.\n- The audio is pushed onto the stack\n- The audio and position are popped from the stack, and an audio event is created.\n- The event is pushed onto the stack.
triggers.BalintHelper/BaseInstructionTrigger/GetTypeInstruction.placements.description.main=- object 'X' is pushed onto the stack\n- 'X' is popped from the stack, and its type is queried\n- The type is pushed onto the stack.
triggers.BalintHelper/GetVariableInfoTrigger/LoadConstantInstruction.placements.description.main=- pushes the variable info stored within the instruction onto the stack\nNote: to actually read or write the value, use Read or Write
triggers.BalintHelper/BaseInstructionTrigger/InitVariableInstruction.placements.description.main=- variable info 'V' is pushed onto the stack\n- object 'X' is pushed onto the stack\n- 'V' and 'X' are popped from the stack, variable 'V' is initialized with 'X'
triggers.BalintHelper/BaseInstructionTrigger/InvokeInstruction.placements.description.main=- an object instance 'N' is pushed onto the stack (if required)\n- arguments 1 through N are pushed onto the stack\n- callable 'M' is pushed onto the stack\n- the method, arguments, and instance are popped from the stack and the call is performed.\n- The result, if any, is pushed onto the stack.
triggers.BalintHelper/BaseInstructionTrigger/IsDefinedInstruction.placements.description.main=- variable info 'V' is pushed onto the stack\n- 'V' is popped from the stack, and a lookup is performed.\n- The boolean result is pushed onto the stack.
triggers.BalintHelper/TypedInstructionTrigger/IsTypeInstruction.placements.description.main=- object 'X' is pushed onto the stack\n- the type of 'X' is compared against the type stored in the instruction.\n- The boolean result is pushed onto the stack.
triggers.BalintHelper/BaseInstructionTrigger/LoadArrayElementInstruction.placements.description.main=- an array instance is pushed onto the stack\n- Indices 1 through N are pushed onto the stack\n- The array and indices are popped from the stack and the array is indexed.\n- The indexed value is pushed onto the stack.
triggers.BalintHelper/LoadPrimitiveInstructionTrigger/LoadConstantInstruction.placements.description.main=- pushes the constant stored within the instruction onto the stack.
triggers.BalintHelper/NewArrayInstructionTrigger/NewArrayInstruction.placements.description.main=- sizes 1 through N are pushed onto the stack\n- sizes are popped from the stack, and an array of dimension N and of the type stored in the instruction is created.\n- The created array is pushed onto the stack.
triggers.BalintHelper/BaseInstructionTrigger/NopInstruction.placements.description.main=Does nothing.
triggers.BalintHelper/BaseInstructionTrigger/PopInstruction.placements.description.main=Pops the value on top of the stack.
triggers.BalintHelper/BaseInstructionTrigger/ReadIndexerInstruction.placements.description.main=- an object instance 'X' is pushed onto the stack (if required)\n- indices 1 through N are pushed onto the stack\n- indexer 'I' is pushed onto the stack\n- the indexer, indices, and instance are popped from the stack and the value at the specified index is read.\n- The result is pushed onto the stack.
triggers.BalintHelper/BaseInstructionTrigger/ReadInstruction.placements.description.main=- an object instance 'X' is pushed onto the stack (if required)\n- the target specifier 'F' (field/property/etc) is pushed onto the stack\n- 'X' and 'F' are popped from the stack and the value is read.\n- The value is pushed onto the stack.
triggers.BalintHelper/TypedInstructionTrigger/ReadPointerInstruction.placements.description.main=- a UIntPtr 'P' is pushed onto the stack\n- 'P' is popped from the stack, and the pointer value is read to the type specified in the instruction\n- the read value is pushed onto the stack
triggers.BalintHelper/BaseInstructionTrigger/ReturnInstruction.placements.description.main=- returns the value (exactly 1) on top of the stack to the caller\n- if the stack is empty, returns void.
triggers.BalintHelper/BaseInstructionTrigger/StoreArrayElementInstruction.placements.description.main=- an object 'X' is pushed onto the stack\n- an array instance is pushed onto the stack\n- Indices 1 through N are pushed onto the stack\n- The object, array and indices are popped from the stack and the 'X' is written into the array at the specified index.
triggers.BalintHelper/BaseInstructionTrigger/StructCopyInstruction.placements.description.main=- a value type 'X' is pushed onto the stack\n- 'X' is popped from the stack and copied.\n- The result is pushed onto the stack.\nNote: for reference types, the object is returned as-is.
triggers.BalintHelper/TryCatchFinallyInstructionTrigger/TryCatchFinallyInstruction.placements.description.main=Invokes the specified methods in 'try', 'catch', and 'finally' blocks respectively. The 'try' method may take any number of arguments (read from the stack). The 'catch' method must take either 1 argument (the exception object), or none. The 'finally' must take 0 arguments.
triggers.BalintHelper/TypeOfInstructionTrigger/LoadConstantInstruction.placements.description.main=- pushes the runtime type instance stored within the instruction onto the stack
triggers.BalintHelper/BaseInstructionTrigger/WriteIndexerInstruction.placements.description.main=- an object instance 'X' is pushed onto the stack (if required)\n- indices 1 through N are pushed onto the stack\n- value 'Y' is pushed onto the stack\n- indexer 'I' is pushed onto the stack\n- the indexer, value, indices, and instance are popped from the stack and the value at the specified index is set to 'Y'.
triggers.BalintHelper/BaseInstructionTrigger/WriteInstruction.placements.description.main=- an object instance 'X' is pushed onto the stack (if required)\n- value 'Y' is pushed onto the stack\n- the target specifier 'F' (field/property/etc) is pushed onto the stack\n- 'F', 'Y', and 'X' are popped from the stack and the value is set to 'Y'.
triggers.BalintHelper/TypedInstructionTrigger/WritePointerInstruction.placements.description.main=- a UIntPtr 'P' is pushed onto the stack\n- an object 'X' is pushed onto the stack\n- 'X' and 'P' are popped from the stack, and the 'P' is written with 'X' as the type specified in the instruction
triggers.BalintHelper/LogInstructionTrigger.placements.description.main=- an object instance 'X' is pushed onto the stack\n- 'X' is popped from the stack and written to the log file
triggers.BalintHelper/IsNullInstructionTrigger/NopInstruction.placements.description.main=a compound instruction to shorten 'Dup' -> 'Primitive (Null)' -> 'Comparison (Equals)'